{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "PRO-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Changing a subscription item credits the unused time of the old item as a negative line: minus the old unit amount times the old quantity times remaining time over period length. The credit carries the discount in force on the credited period, a used once coupon included.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "dev fixtures with a subscription coupon (builder report); RECON.md's 'credit not discounted' holds only for a coupon passed to the preview"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-02",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "It charges the remaining time on the new item as a positive line: new unit amount times new quantity times remaining time over period length.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "RECON.md: +2000"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-03",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Proration is computed to the second from proration_date to the end of the current period.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-04",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Rounding of a prorated amount exactly at half a cent differs by mode: credits round away from zero; a classic charge of 5555555.5 is charged 5555555 (dev-brk-big-half-charge-classic), not rounded half up.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "builder pass v2 notes (clone/NOTES.md), checked against the dev fixtures named"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-05",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Without an immediate invoice, the preview is the next renewal invoice: prorations plus the next full period at the new price and quantity.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "RECON.md: 3000 next-period line"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-06",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "proration_behavior=none together with a proration_date is rejected: 'Cannot specify proration date if no proration is being done'.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "d-behavior-none, d-pct20-none (builder report 2026-09-23); the documented behaviour without a date is not probed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-07",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "proration_behavior=always_invoice previews an immediate invoice holding only the proration lines.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-08",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A quantity change prorates like a price change: credit at the old quantity, charge at the new quantity.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/quantities"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-09",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A downgrade gives a negative proration total; a negative invoice total leaves amount_due at 0 and the remainder as customer credit.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/customer/balance"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO-10",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A price change sent without a quantity bills quantity 1 on the new item, not the old quantity.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "mined",
        "ref": "builder, from rand-004 and rand-011 (dev)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PER-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A monthly period runs to the same day of the next calendar month, so the period length in seconds depends on the month.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/billing-cycle"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "INT-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Interval changes. Flexible mode: monthly to yearly prorates the yearly price over the remaining time and keeps the anchor; yearly to monthly keeps the anchor while the proration date is inside the new monthly period and is rejected past it. Classic mode: an interval change resets the billing cycle to the clock time. Yearly to yearly keeps the period. In flexible mode each item keeps its own billing period; a proration date exactly at the new period end is accepted. Classic mode refuses mixed intervals, and flexible mixed intervals refuse a forever amount-off coupon.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "t-month-to-year-*, u-year-to-month-*, u-year-to-year (dev); builder pass 3 (dev fixtures), clone/NOTES.md pass 6; edited 2026-09-23 after the final measurement, statements only"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DSC-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A percent-off coupon takes round(percent × sum) from the discountable lines it applies to and spreads it across them by a running rounded-down total: each line gets floor(running share) minus what earlier lines already got. This includes the first invoice, whose allocation sets the discount a flexible credit carries (wide3-256 for four lines).",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "builder pass v2 notes (clone/NOTES.md), checked against the dev fixtures named"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DSC-02",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "In flexible billing mode, the discount is applied inside proration lines (proration_discounts=included) instead of at invoice level.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "RECON.md: 1600 'with 20.0% off' line"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DSC-03",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "An amount-off coupon is allocated across discountable lines in proportion to their amounts, with rounding.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "documented",
        "ref": "https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations (166/334 example)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DSC-04",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Classic mode: proration lines are not discountable. The credit is -round_half_away(net × r/P), where net is the old item's amount after applying, in subscription order and to that item alone, every discount on the subscription when the credited period was billed: an amount-off in full, a percent-off as round(pct × what is left), never below 0. The share each discount got on the billing invoice is irrelevant, a share of 0 included. The charge prorates first and subtracts the prorated discount after.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "spent batch 3, analysed in analysis/hold-b3-failures.md (2026-10-13), and dev fixtures"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DSC-05",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A once coupon is used up only by an invoice where it actually took something off; a subscription's once coupon that took nothing stays active (dev-brk-free-once, wide3-027, -054, -230, -249). A once coupon passed to the preview discounts the remaining-time charge and is then used up, so it no longer discounts the renewal; when the change prorates nothing it discounts the renewal and is listed; in an immediate invoice it is listed at 0.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "observed",
        "ref": "builder pass v2 notes (clone/NOTES.md), checked against the dev fixtures named"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "MOD-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "Classic and flexible modes differ by the order of prorating and discounting (DSC-02, DSC-04), which can move a line by one cent, by the credit line's discount list for a used once coupon, and by the cycle reset on an interval change in classic mode, and by the remaining-time line of a new item billed at 0 (PRO-11).",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "mined",
        "ref": "builder pass 3 (dev fixtures), clone/NOTES.md pass 6; edited 2026-09-23 after the final measurement, statements only"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ERR-01",
      "area": "logic",
      "statement": "A proration_date outside the allowed window is rejected with an invalid_request_error.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "inferred",
        "ref": "API reference, proration_date parameter"
